{"timestamp":"2026-07-12T21:22:30.751Z","ordinal":359,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","call_id":"call_Ey8iNVkvCcLBfnAk3BXGYsYq","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"How can I license Houdini Engine Indie? | SideFX (https://www.sidefx.com/faq/question/how-do-i-license-houdini-engine-indie/)\nciteturn2search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; If you would like to use the Houdini software interactively, you can purchase Houdini Indie here: www.sidefx.com/buy ... Licensing Houdini Engine is the same as licensing other Houdini products.\n\n##### How can I license Houdini Engine Indie?\n\n    \n\nLicensing a non-graphical version of Houdini-Indie\n\n* * *\n\nThe Houdini-Engine-Indie license is a 3-part license consisting of:\n\n  * Houdini Engine Indie\n  * Render (Non-Commercial)\n  * Karma (Non-Commercial)\n\nThe Houdini-Engine-Indie is a non-graphical version of Houdini-Indie. It allows you to run command-line renders, and simulations, on remote render machines. It can also open pre-made Houdini Digital Assets (HDAs) within Maya, Unreal, Unity and C4D. You make best use of your Houdini-Engine-Indie license if it is installed on a different machine than your Houdini-Indie license.\n\nIf you would like to use the Houdini software interactively, you can purchase Houdini Indie here: www.sidefx.com/buy\n\nTo install a license of Houdini Engine Indie, please see HERE for more information.\n\nLicensing Houdini Engine is the same as licensing other Houdini products.\n\nFor Game Studios, please see our Houdini Engine For Game Studios guide.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHoudini Engine | SideFX (https://www.sidefx.com/products/houdini-engine/)\nciteturn2search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Customers can access up to 10 of these licenses per studio through the SideFX website, and request as many as they need through their account manager. ... #### FREE Houdini Engine Indie ... Assets created in Houdini Apprentice can be deployed in school labs using Houdini Engine Education to load them into Host apps.\n\n# PIPELINE TOOLS\n\n## Studio Wide Solutions\n\nHoudini Engine supports a deep integration of Houdini and its procedural workflow within the larger framework of a Studio pipeline. Houdini Engine functions as both a plug-in to other applications and a non-graphical solution for batch processing and distributing important tasks to the farm.\n\nENGINE FOR FILM/TV PDF                     ENGINE FOR GAMES PDF\n\n## HOUDINI ENGINE PLUG-INS\n\nHoudini Engine brings a procedural node-based approach to your favorite app. Build networks that define a recipe that can be applied over and over, then wrap them up to create custom smart assets. Share these assets with colleagues who can load them directly into 3D apps such as Autodesk® Maya® or Autodesk® 3ds Max® or into game editors such as Unity® or Unreal Engine.®\n\nImage\n\nSuki & the Shadow Klaw | Feline Arts\n\nIN HOUDINI | In Houdini, everything you do creates a node. These nodes are wired together into networks which define a flow of data which make it easy to go back and make changes. Networks can also be encapsulated into single nodes called Houdini Digital Assets which are easy to share with colleagues. These assets provide artist-built tools that brings procedural solutions to your pipelines.\n\nImage\n\nProcedural Bridge Asset in Unity Game Engine\n\nIN HOST APPLICATION | Houdini Engine lets you load Houdini Digital Assets into other 3D apps. Any parameters added to the asset are available for editing and handles can be set up in the viewport for interactive manipulation. One asset can be used multiple times in a level or in multiple levels. Changes made to the core asset, even deep into production, will update all instantiations of the asset.\n\n# HOW HOUDINI ENGINE WORKS\n\n* * *\n\nImage\n\n# BATCH\n\n## PROCESSING\n\nThe Houdini Engine can also be used to Batch Process Houdini in non-graphical mode on the farm.  You can use Houdini Engine licenses in batch mode to distribute a wide range of important tasks such as rendering, dynamic simulation, motion and geometry caching.\n\nLEARN MORE\n\n#### INDIE\n\nImage\n\n#### Houdini Engine\n\nHoudini Engine licenses let you run the plug-ins and batch process on computers which don't have access to interactive licenses. They offer a more affordable solution for larger pipelines.\n\nBUY NOW!\n\nImage        Image\n\n#### FREE for Unreal/Unity\n\nHoudini Engine for Unreal and Unity are now available for commercial customers for free.  Customers can access up to 10 of these licenses per studio through the SideFX website, and request as many as they need through their account manager. \n\nBUY NOW!\n\nImage\n\n#### FREE Houdini Engine Indie\n\nHoudini Engine Indie offers a way for indie artists to have free access to running the plug-ins or batch processing on up to 3 computers which don't have access to interactive licenses. \n\nDOWNLOAD NOW!\n\n#### LEARNING WITH APPRENTICE\n\nAssets created in Houdini Apprentice can be deployed in school labs using Houdini Engine Education to load them into Host apps.\n\nHobbyists or artists working at home, should consider working with Houdini Indie to work with the Engine Plug-ins.\n\nCompare Products\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow does Houdini Engine licensing work? | SideFX (https://www.sidefx.com/faq/question/how-does-houdini-engine-licensing-work/)\nciteturn2search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Artists with Houdini Core or Houdini FX licenses will be able to run the Houdini Engine using their existing licenses. ... Licensing Houdini Engine is the same as licensing any Houdini license, please see HERE for more information. ...  | Houdini Engine  | Houdini Engine Indie  | Houdini Engine Education  | Houdini Engine for Unity and Unreal\n\n##### How does Houdini Engine licensing work?\n\n    \n\nBuying, setting up, and managing Houdini Engine licenses\n\n* * *\n\n## Overview\n\nArtists with Houdini Core or Houdini FX licenses will be able to run the Houdini Engine using their existing licenses. For artists who only need to work with a Houdini Engine plugin, batch processing, or custom HAPI integration in another application, a Houdini Engine license serves this purpose.\n\n## Pricing\n\nHoudini Engine workstation licenses will be available for $525 annually while floating licenses for use in a single facility will start at $795 annually. Volume pricing will be available for floating licenses. For commercial users using the Houdini Engine Unreal plugin or the Houdini Engine Unity plugin, there is a free license that can be obtained on our Buy page.\n\n## Licensing\n\nLicensing Houdini Engine is the same as licensing any Houdini license, please see HERE for more information.\n\nFor Game Studios, please see our Houdini Engine For Game Studios guide.\n\n## Houdini Engine Compatibility\n\nThe various Houdini Engine licenses are intended to be used with their corresponding Houdini license. Please use the chart below to understand which one to acquire.\n\n | Houdini Engine  | Houdini Engine Indie  | Houdini Engine Education  | Houdini Engine for Unity and Unreal\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\n Houdini FX  | ✅  | ❌  | ❌  | ✅\nHoudini Core   | ✅  | ❌  | ❌  | ✅\n Houdini Indie\n | ❌  | ✅  | ❌  | ❌\nHoudini Education   | ❌  | ❌  | ✅  | ❌\n\nNOTE:\n\n> Houdini Apprentice is only compatible with Houdini Engine Education. This is because both Houdini Apprentice and Houdini Education save digital assets in the non-commercial .hdanc format. Houdini Engine Education in included with Houdini Education purchases and cannot be purchased separately.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLicensing | SideFX (https://www.sidefx.com/Support/licensing/)\nciteturn2search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; After installing Houdini, you can set up the licensing path depending on which product and which license type you choose. ... While there are a number of different SideFX products including Houdini, Houdini Indie, Houdini Education, Houdini Engine, or Karma they all come from the same install.\n\nHoudini products can be licensed in different ways to meet the needs of individual artists, studios and schools. After installing Houdini, you can set up the licensing path depending on which product and which license type you choose.\n\n## INSTALLATION\n\nImage\n\nWhile there are a number of different SideFX products including Houdini, Houdini Indie, Houdini Education, Houdini Engine, or Karma they all come from the same install. Whether you use the Launcher or the Installer, you install Houdini then let your license determine which part of the software you are accessing. \n\nNote that the HQUEUE Software and SideFX Labs can be installed independently.\n\nDownload Launcher\n\n## PRODUCT LICENSES\n\nThere are a number of Houdini products that meet the needs of commercial, indie [limited commercial] and education [non-commercial] customers. Each of these categories is designed to work as a family of products that function as a complete pipeline. It is important to get the right products for your chosen category. \n\n## \n\n## Commercial Products\n\nHoudini CORE / Houdini FX / Houdini ENGINE\n\nCommercial Artists and Studios\n\nFile Formats |  .hip/.hda/.usd\n\nThese licenses are for Studios and Artists doing commercial work. There are a number of different ways to license these products to suit your specific needs. Learn how each license works and how to set up the relevant license servers.\n\nHow to LICENSE\n\n## \n\n## Indie Products \n\nHoudini INDIE /  Houdini ENGINE INDIE\n\nIndie Artists making less than $100k USD\n\nFile Formats |  .hiplc/.hdalc/.usd\n\nThe Indie licenses are for artists making less than $100K USD or working with less than $1 million USD in funding. These are workstation licenses that can be set up in one of two ways. Learn how to set up your licenses and how to get started quickly.\n\nHow to LICENSE\n\n## \n\n## Education Products\n\nHoudini EDUCATION / Houdini ENGINE EDUCATION\n\nStudents, Schools and Training Centres\n\nFile Formats | .hipnc/.hdanc/.usd\n\nEducation licenses are available for individual students or for computer labs in schools. Learn how to set up different license servers for these situations. These are non-commercial licenses that can only be used for teaching and for learning.\n\nHow to LICENSE\n\n## \n\n## Try Houdini for FREE\n\nHoudini APPRENTICE\n\nHobbyists and Students \n\nFile Formats | .hipnc/.hdanc/.usdnc\n\nHoudini Apprentice is a trial version that can be used to explore the features of Houdini while completing non-commercial projects. Apprentice is licensed differently than other versions of Houdini to make it quick and easy to set up.\n\nLEARN MORE\n\n## LICENSE TYPES\n\nWhen you purchase a Houdini license, you can choose between different license types that determine whether you lock your licenses to one computer or share throughout your studio.\n\n  * Workstation [Node-Locked] – This license type can be used on a single computer and can only be accessed either from a local server or from logging in to SideFX.com.\n\n  * Local Access [Floating] – These licenses can be set up on a server and shared with a team of artists within a 100KM distance from each other. When an artist starts Houdini a license is checked out of the server as long as there is one available. Local licenses are designed for a single location.\n\n  * Global Access [Floating] – These licenses can be set up on a server and shared with a team of artists around the world. When an artist starts Houdini a license is checked out of the server as long as there is one available. Global licenses are for sharing between studios in different locations.\n\nCOMMERCIAL\n\nINDIE\n\nEDUCATION\n\nAPPRENTICE\n\nUSER\n\nStudios/Artists\n\nIndie Artists\n\nSchools/Students\n\nTrial/Hobbyists/Students\n\nLICENSE TYPES\n\nWorkstation\n\nLocal Access [LAL]\n\nGlobal Access [GAL]\n\nWorkstation\n\n Global Access [GAL]\n\nWorkstation\n\n## HQUEUE\n\nHQUEUE is a general-purpose job scheduling system that is included with Houdini. HQUEUE is designed to distribute, monitor and manage tasks across a collection of computing nodes, or client machines. \n\nIt specializes in managing render and dynamic simulation jobs submitted from Houdini, but you can customize it to work with any job from any application.\n\nHQUEUE works with commercial, indie and educational Houdini. You can use Houdini or PDG/TOPS to set up distributed tasks then the client machines will consume Houdini Engine and/or Karma licenses.\n\nAbout HQUEUE--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHoudini Engine 8.0: Licensing (https://www.sidefx.com/docs/hengine/_h_a_p_i__licensing.html)\nciteturn2search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 days ago; Crawled: 3 days ago; Apprentice) are not supported. ... Indie license usage is limited to authorized plugins (Unity, Unreal, Maya, Max, C4D). ... You can force Houdini Engine to only checkout interactive licenses, that is: Houdini, Houdini FX, or Houdini Indie, so even if there is a Houdini Engine license available but no interactive licenses available, Houdini Engine will fail the license check.\nHoudini Engine 8.0\n\nLicensing\n\n### Table of Contents\n\n  * License Requirements\n  * License Checks\n\n# License Requirements\n\nHoudini Engine will check for these licenses, in this order, until one is found:\n\n  1. Houdini Engine\n  2. Houdini Core\n  3. Houdini FX\n  4. Houdini Engine Indie\n  5. Houdini Indie\n\nNon-commercial licenses (ie. Apprentice) are not supported. Furthermore, tainting - the process of instantiating an asset created with a lower tier license while using a higher tier license - is not allowed within Houdini Engine. This means, for example, that you cannot run Indie (*lc) assets in Engine while using a commercial license - you will need to checkout an Indie license to run Indie assets. That said, lower tier licenses can run assets created with a higher tier license. For example, Houdini Engine running on an Indie license can run commercial assets. Indie license usage is limited to authorized plugins (Unity, Unreal, Maya, Max, C4D).\n\nYou also limit which license Houdini Engine can use. You can force Houdini Engine to only checkout interactive licenses, that is: Houdini, Houdini FX, or Houdini Indie, so even if there is a Houdini Engine license available but no interactive licenses available, Houdini Engine will fail the license check. The opposite is also possible. You can force Houdini Engine to only checkout engine licenses, that is: Houdini Engine or Houdini Engine Indie. This is achieved via the `HAPI_LICENSE_MODE` environment variable. See Environment Variables.\n\n# License Checks\n\nHoudini Engine will check for a valid license during two sets of API calls:\n\n  1. During library file loading: Asset Library Files\n  2. During node creation: Node Creation and Create Node\n\nDuring library file loading, you can get the following HAPI_Result's if no valid license is found:\n\n  1. HAPI_RESULT_NO_LICENSE_FOUND - Simply no licenses were found, at all.\n  2. HAPI_RESULT_DISALLOWED_NC_LICENSE_FOUND - Only unsupported non-commercial licenses were found.\n\nDuring node creation, you can get the following HAPI_Result's regarding licenses. Note that if you are in threaded mode, these results will be available as cook results. See Cooking.\n\n  1. HAPI_RESULT_NO_LICENSE_FOUND - Simply no licenses were found, at all.\n  2. HAPI_RESULT_DISALLOWED_NC_LICENSE_FOUND - Only unsupported non-commercial licenses were found.\n  3. HAPI_RESULT_DISALLOWED_NC_ASSET_WITH_C_LICENSE - Since no tainting is allowed, non-commercial assets cannot run with a commercial license.\n  4. HAPI_RESULT_DISALLOWED_NC_ASSET_WITH_LC_LICENSE - Since no tainting is allowed, non-commercial assets cannot run with a limited-commercial license.\n  5. HAPI_RESULT_DISALLOWED_LC_ASSET_WITH_C_LICENSE - Since no tainting is allowed, limited commercial assets cannot run with a commercial license.\n  6. HAPI_RESULT_DISALLOWED_HENGINEINDIE_W_3PARTY_PLUGIN - Indie license can only be used with authorized plugins.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWhat Houdini Engine license do I need? | SideFX (https://www.sidefx.com/faq/question/what-houdini-engine-license-do-i-need/)\nciteturn2search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Houdini Engine for Unity/Unreal provides free commercial licenses for the UE5 and Unity plug-ins only. ... Houdini Engine Indie  | FREE  | .\n\nFrom Houdini 18.5\n\n##### What Houdini Engine license do I need?\n\n    \n\nHoudini Engine for Unity/Unreal provides free commercial licenses for the UE5 and Unity plug-ins only.\n\nFor all other host applications, including proprietary plug-ins, and for Batch processing on the farm, commercial Houdini Engine licenses are available for rent. These licenses are also available as volume rentals for medium and large studios.\n\nLicense  | Cost  | Asset Types  | Houdini GUI  | UE5 Plug-in  | Unity Plug-in  | Maya/Max Plug-in  | Batch Processing\nHoudini Engine for Unity  | FREE  | .HDA  | x  | YES  | YES  | x  | x\nHoudini Engine for UE5  | FREE  | .HDA  | x  | YES  | YES  | x  | x\nHoudini Engine  | $$  | .HDA  | x  | YES  | YES  | YES  | YES\nHoudini Engine Indie  | FREE  | .HDALC/.HDA  | x  | YES  | YES  | YES  | YES--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEducation licence: how to use Houdini Engine for Unreal | Forums | SideFX (https://www.sidefx.com/forum/topic/94358/)\nciteturn2search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.4 years ago; Crawled: last week; See the compare page for more info. https://www.sidefx.com/products/compare/ [www.sidefx.com] ... I want to know whether indie license holder can use .hda file in Unreal with houdini engine.\nGet rid of the free Houdini Engine for Unreal/Unity and then your education license will be used for the HE for Unreal and the .hdanc file will be accepted.\nRobert\n\nMarkWoo\n    Member\n    Image\n    1 posts\n    Joined: Nov. 2023\n    Offline\n\n Jan. 14, 2026 3 p.m.\n\n> rmagee\n> Does anyone have the free Houdini Engine for Unreal/Unity installed? This a commercial license that will interfere with education licenses. What happens is that when you open up Unreal it finds the commercial license then when you load an education asset it is rejected because those files aren't allow in commercial software.\n> Get rid of the free Houdini Engine for Unreal/Unity and then your education license will be used for the HE for Unreal and the .hdanc file will be accepted.\n> Robert\n\nHello thanks for this information. I want to know whether indie license holder can use .hda file in Unreal with houdini engine. Will houdini engine for indie license only support .hdalc file in unreal? Also for apprentice license holder, whether their houdini engine only support .hdanc file in unreal?\n\nrmagee\n    Staff\n    Image\n    1431 posts\n    Joined: July 2005\n    Offline\n\n Jan. 15, 2026 11:35 a.m.\n\nIf you are using Houdini Indie then you need to be using Houdini Engine for Indie. Again No Houdini Engine for Unreal/Unity because that will be the default license grabbed by Unreal and it cannot open .hdalc files.\nThe Houdini Engine for Indie will open both .hdalc and .hda files but not .hdanc.\n\nRobert Magee--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWhich licenses are needed to run which product? | SideFX (https://www.sidefx.com/faq/question/which-license-strings-are-required-for-each-houdini-product/)\nciteturn2search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; The following table illustrates shows the license string required for each product type: ... Houdini Engine Indie  | Houdini Engine Indie  | 1 ... Non-Commercial  | Houdini Apprentice  | WS  | Houdini FX (Non-Commercial)  | 1\n\n##### Which licenses are needed to run which product?\n\n    \n\nThe following table illustrates shows the license string required for each product type:\nNote: Renderer is Mantra renderer.\n\nLicense Category  | Product Name  | License Type  | Product License String  | Default Qty\nCommercial  | Houdini Core | FX  | WS  | Houdini Core | Houdini FX  | 1\nRenderer  | 5\nKarma Renderer  | 5\nHoudini Core | FX  | LAL|GAL  | Houdini Core | Houdini FX  | 1\nRenderer  | 10\nKarma Renderer  | 10\nHoudini Engine  | WS|GAL  | Houdini Engine  | 1\nRenderer  | 1\nHoudini Engine for Unity/Unreal  | GAL  | Houdini-Engine-PlugIn-Free  | 1\nLimited Commercial  | Houdini Indie  | WS  | Houdini Indie  | 2\nRenderer (Non-Commercial)  | 2\nKarma Renderer (Non-Commercial)  | 2\nHoudini Engine Indie  | Houdini Engine Indie  | 1\nRenderer (Non-Commercial)  | 1\nEducational  | Houdini Education  | GAL  | Houdini Education  | 1\nHoudini Engine Education  | 10\nRenderer (Non-Commercial)  | 10\nKarma Renderer (Non-Commercial)  | 10\nHoudini Education for Students  | Houdini Education  | 1\nHoudini Engine Education  | 1\nRenderer (Non-Commercial)  | 10\nKarma Renderer (Non-Commercial)  | 10\nHoudini Engine Education  | Houdini Engine Education  | 1\nRenderer (Non-Commercial)  | 1\nNon-Commercial  | Houdini Apprentice  | WS  | Houdini FX (Non-Commercial)  | 1\nRenderer (Non-Commercial)  | 1\nKarma Renderer (Non-Commercial)  | 1\n\n  * Commercial Karma Renderer and Renderer are always GAL.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHoudini license system (https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/licensing/system.html)\nciteturn2search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; SideFX license system is per machine not per application. ... For example, Houdini FX cannot checkout a Houdini Engine license. ... -core  | Add `--check-licenses=\"Houdini-Escape\"`, `--skip-licenses=\"Houdini-Master`, and `--skip-license-modes=\"education,indie,apprentice\"` ... Houdini 19 licensing uses HTTP(S) exclusively and will make NO no attempt at providing any backwards compatibility in behavior of the old system or in communication protocol with the old system.\n\n# Houdini license system\n\nOn this page  | \n\n  * Product Exchanging\n  * Command line options\n  * Environment variables\n  * Guide to moving to Houdini 19 Licensing System\n\nThe license products are ordered based on a hierarchy. The hierarchy is based on the financial cost and features available for that product (i.e. FX > Core > Engine). The system works based on a list of lists. Each sub list represents a license mode (Commercial, Education, Indie, Non Commercial). The order of the lists also tells hserver which are more important and which are less important (the first sublist being the most important). The order of the sublists are `[Commercial, Education, Indie, Non Commercial]`.\n\nHython License List\n    \n    [\n    [Engine, Core, FX],\n    [Engine EDU, EDU],\n    [Engine Indie, Indie],\n    [Apprentice]\n    ]\n\nLicense Mode  | License List\n--- | ---\nCommercial  | Engine, Core, FX\nEducation  | Engine EDU, EDU\nIndie  | Engine Indie, Indie\nApprentice  | Apprentice\n\nIn this example the list of lists can be transformed into `[Engine, Core, FX, Engine EDU, EDU, Engine Indie, Indie, Apprentice]` as another way of thinking about the license checkout order. For example, Houdini FX cannot checkout a Houdini Engine license.\n\nTip\n\nIf running Houdini Core and Houdini FX at the same time is common its recommended to add `--check-licenses=\"Houdini-Master\"` to Houdini Core environment variable. See below for details.\n\n`--skip-licenses`\n\nWith some setups it might be desired to skip certain licenses for a number of different reasons. A studio might reserve FX licenses for specific roles or projects and might want everyone else to use Core in the meantime. In some cases it might make sense that an artist never wants to grab a Houdini Non Commercial license. With this option specific licenses can be skipped. The syntax for this option is `--skip-licenses=\"Houdini-Non-Commercial\"` with `,` being the separator between license names.\n\n`--skip-license-modes`\n\nThis option allows entire license categories to be skipped when requesting a license. This option can be handy when a user does not want to checkout a non-commercial license. `commercial`, `education`, `indie`, and `apprentice` are the available options.\nSome values have been omitted as they no longer apply with this new system.\n\nHOUDINI_SCRIPT_LICENSE  | Houdini 19 Environment Options\n--- | ---\nhbatch -R  | Add `--skip-licenses=\"Houdini-Escape,Houdini-Master\"`\nPDG_LICENSE_MODE  | Houdini 19 Environment Options\n--- | ---\npdg_only  | No action should be taken as this just uses the existing pdg license list when the application uses one (i.e. PilotPDG).\nengine_only  | Add `--check-licenses=\"Houdini-Engine\"` and `--skip-licenses=\"Houdini-Escape,Houdini-Master\"`.\nhoudini_core_only  | Add `--check-licenses=\"Houdini-Escape\"` and `--skip-licenses=\"Houdini-Engine,Houdini-Master\"`.\nhoudini_fx_only  | Add `--check-licenses=\"Houdini-Master\"` and `--skip-licenses=\"Houdini-Escape,Houdini-Engine\"`.\nHoudini command line  | Houdini 19 Options\n--- | ---\n-apprentice  | Add `--skip-license-modes=commercial,education,indie`\n-indie  | Add `--skip-license-modes=commercial,education,apprentice`\n-core  | Add `--check-licenses=\"Houdini-Escape\"`, `--skip-licenses=\"Houdini-Master`, and `--skip-license-modes=\"education,indie,apprentice\"`\n\nHoudini 19 licensing goes from hserver and a complex network of environment variables controlling behavior to the application deciding the full list of licenses that it should be allowed to use. As such hserver options `--relax-non-graphical/-g` and `--render-only/-n` are no longer used with this system. These options can still be set for applications using the old system but will simply be ignored for this system as they are not necessary as the application controls the licensing behavior for Houdini 19 licensing.\n\nHoudini 19 licensing uses HTTP(S) exclusively and will make NO no attempt at providing any backwards compatibility in behavior of the old system or in communication protocol with the old system. Hserver is able to run using both systems at the same time but upgrading/downgrading will be disabled as hserver is unable to make a decision on what to do as older systems will not provide the necessary information.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHoudini Engine for unreal for commercial project | Forums | SideFX (https://www.sidefx.com/forum/topic/78081/)\nciteturn2search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.4 years ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Do I need to buy a license for Houdini Indie, or I can use HOUDINI APPRENTICE to make asset and export to unreal for free even the project is commercial? ... To create an asset for commercial use (.hda) you will need either Houdini Core or Houdini FX to feed the new free Houdini Engine for Unreal license. ... SideFX\n\n### Houdini Engine for unreal for commercial project\n\n   2801   1   0\n\n1manarmyworkshop\n    Member\n    Image\n    2 posts\n    Joined: Feb. 2021\n    Offline\n\n Feb. 28, 2021 11 p.m.\n\nHoudini Engine is free plugin for unreal now. But if I need to use HDA Asset in unreal for commercial project. Do I need to buy a license for Houdini Indie, or I can use HOUDINI APPRENTICE to make asset and export to unreal for free even the project is commercial?\n\nrmagee\n    Staff\n    Image\n    1431 posts\n    Joined: July 2005\n    Offline\n\n March 1, 2021 12:32 a.m.\n\nTo create an asset for commercial use (.hda) you will need either Houdini Core or Houdini FX to feed the new free Houdini Engine for Unreal license.\nFor limited commercial use (.hdalc) (Your company makes less than $100K USD) then you can use Houdini Indie with Houdini Engine Indie (up to three).\nApprentice (.hdanc) is for learning Houdini and the only way to use it with Unreal is in a school setting where the school has Houdini Engine Education licenses.\nYou cannot mix Apprentice, Indie or commercial products in the same pipeline. You have to go one way or the other.\n\nRobert Magee\nSenior Product Marketing Manager\nSideFX--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub - sideeffects/HoudiniEngineForUnreal: Houdini Engine Plugin for Unreal Engine. · GitHub (https://github.com/sideeffects/HoudiniEngineForUnreal)\nciteturn2search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: last month; sideeffects / HoudiniEngineForUnreal Public ...  Houdini21.0-Unreal5.00 ... In this GitHub repository, click Releases on the right side. ... Get the UE source code from: https://github.com/EpicGames/UnrealEngine/releases\n# Feedback\n\nPlease send bug reports, feature requests and questions to Side FX's support.\n\n# Compatibility\n\nCurrently, the plugins has binaries that have been built for UE5.6, UE5.5, and is linked with the latest production build of Houdini.\n\nSource code for the plugin is available on this repository for UE5.\n\n> Please note that all UE5.X versions of the plugin use the same source files/branches, the sources in the 5.0 branch are also intended to be used with more recent versions of the plugin (ie 5.6 , 5.5 etc.)\n\nIn general, we support the latest two releases of UE5.X, but will try to make the source code compatible with previous versions of Unreal.\n\n> For Houdini 21.0 - there is now two versions of the plugins: one with PCG support and one without PCG. Supporting PCG means that the Houdini Engine plugin now needs to depend on the PCG plugin, which is still considered experimental by Epic. We provide both versions of the plugin with your Houdini install and on this repo's release page, but the source code available here is with PCG support enabled. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNanite Foliage | Unreal Engine 5.8 Documentation | Epic Developer Community (https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/unreal-engine/nanite-foliage)\nciteturn2search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Nanite foliage makes use of old and new techniques to render open worlds with large open vistas at higher quality at a fraction of the original frame costs, with instancing, skinned meshes, voxelization, animation, and material characteristics.\n# Nanite Foliage\n\nAn overview of Nanite Foliage and its rendering pipeline.\n\n\nLearn to use this Experimental feature, but use caution when shipping with it.\n\nNanite Foliage is a set of integral systems using Nanite’s virtualized geometry rendering to achieve dense, highly-detailed foliage at scale. Nanite foliage makes use of old and new techniques to render open worlds with large open vistas at higher quality at a fraction of the original frame costs, with instancing, skinned meshes, voxelization, animation, and material characteristics. When combined, this allows for more robust worlds to be imagined with lifelike and animated foliage.\n\n\nA flythrough of The Witcher 4 Technical Demo forest rendered using Nanite Foliage.\n\nTo understand the goals of Nanite Foliage and where it’s headed, it’s important to understand that what has worked in the past isn't efficient for the future in creating these types of fully realized worlds. \n\nLet’s look at some of the ways that the “old way” of developing foliage doesn’t work well for Nanite Foliage:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n00_cover.indd (https://www.sidefx.com/media/uploads/tutorial/foundations_gdc2018/houdini_foundations.pdf)\nciteturn2search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.2 years ago; on the SideFX.com website. ... Houdini Engi